+# User Journey — Current Sprint: Sprint 4
+
+> **Living document.** Updated when UI changes. See `docs/checkpoints/` for snapshots.  
+> **Last updated:** S4_2
+
+---
+
+## Overview
+
+Sprint 4 introduces the web UI. Users can now manage tasks through a browser
+without Postman or curl.
+
+---
+
+## Journey 1: Add a New Task
+
+**User goal:** Create a task with a title and optional description.
+
+```mermaid
+journey
+    title Journey 1: Add a New Task
+    section Navigate
+        Open browser: 5: User
+        Redirect to /tasks/new: 3: System
+    section Fill Form
+        See Add Task form: 5: User
+        Enter title and description: 5: User
+    section Submit
+        Click Add Task button: 5: User
+        Server creates task: 3: System
+        Redirect to task list: 3: System
+    section Verify
+        See task in list: 5: User
+```
+
+| Step | User Action | System Response | HTTP |
+|------|-------------|-----------------|------|
+| 1 | Opens browser → navigates to app | Redirect to `/tasks/new` | 302 |
+| 2 | Sees Add Task form | `GET /tasks/new` → renders `add_task.html` | 200 |
+| 3 | Enters title (required) + description | HTML5 `required` prevents empty submission | — |
+| 4 | Clicks **Add Task** | `POST /tasks/new` → `TaskService.add_task()` → DB | 302 |
+| 5 | Sees task in list | `GET /tasks` → renders `task_list.html` | 200 |
+
+**Validation path (empty title):**
+- User submits empty title → server-side validation catches it → form re-renders with error message
+
+---
+
+## Journey 2: Complete a Task
+
+**User goal:** Mark an existing task as done.
+
+| Step | User Action | System Response | HTTP |
+|------|-------------|-----------------|------|
+| 1 | Views task list at `/tasks` | All tasks rendered | 200 |
+| 2 | Clicks **Complete** button | `POST /tasks/<id>/complete` | — |
+| 3 | `ui.py` calls `TaskService.complete_task(id)` | DB sets `completed = True` | — |
+| 4 | Redirected to task list | 302 → `GET /tasks` | 200 |
+| 5 | Task shows with strikethrough styling | CSS `.task-completed` applied | — |
+
+---
+
+## Journey 3: Delete a Task
+
+**User goal:** Remove a task permanently.
+
+| Step | User Action | System Response | HTTP |
+|------|-------------|-----------------|------|
+| 1 | Views task list at `/tasks` | All tasks rendered | 200 |
+| 2 | Clicks **Delete** button | `POST /tasks/<id>/delete` | — |
+| 3 | `ui.py` calls `TaskService.delete_task(id)` | DB removes row | — |
+| 4 | Redirected to task list | 302 → `GET /tasks` | 200 |
+| 5 | Task no longer appears | `get_all_tasks()` returns updated list | — |
+
+---
+
+## Technical Pattern: Post-Redirect-Get (PRG)
+
+All form submissions follow the Post-Redirect-Get pattern:
+1. **POST** — form submitted, action taken
+2. **Redirect** — 302 response
+3. **GET** — browser loads fresh page
+
+This prevents duplicate form submissions if the user refreshes after an action.
+
+---
+
+## Validation: Defense in Depth
+
+| Layer | Mechanism | Catches |
+|-------|-----------|---------|
+| Front-end | HTML5 `required` attribute | Empty title in browser |
+| Back-end (UI) | `ui.py` server-side check | Bypassed front-end validation |
+| Back-end (Service) | `TaskService.add_task()` ValueError | Invalid data from any source |
+| Database | `NOT NULL` constraint | Direct DB writes without service layer |
